notes:QUEUED EXECUTION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: Build the closed swift-v1/swift-repository-v1 design from accepted TASK-260728-2spy93, TASK-260728-1g0z69 and TASK-260729-rhjxtx evidence. Complete every reserved Swift registry field and acceptance layer: trusted root/swiftc identity, version and unversioned target normalization, SDK/toolchain/stdlib closure, tested compatibility families, metadata disposition for swift-tools-version and .swift-version, deterministic artifact/cache/receipt/marker identity, and fail-before-compiler diagnostics. Define one fixed manager-owned graph for local build_roots and exact external skill-build.json targets. Exhaustively decide Package.swift/Package.resolved/dependency vendoring/products/targets/configurations/plugins/macros/scripts/binary and system-library targets/C-C++ interop/unsafeFlags/env/network/linker/SDK selection; package code must not execute manifest programs or select scripts/plugins/macros/network/native inputs outside the contract. Preserve measured distinction between target representability and stdlib availability and measured compilation evidence. macOS is primary; Windows contract must be implementation-ready without false native qualification; Linux remains later qualification. Preserve frozen release bytes, no stage/commit/publish/pin, hand off with deterministic decision/reference/vector/probe evidence.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-ce039d, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-ce039d)\nCONTINUATION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: RUN-260728-ce039d was operator-cancelled after about nine minutes solely to prioritize critical curator-spec rework; this is not a defect or scope change. Resume the original Swift driver-pair design from the preserved task worktree and existing reconnaissance instead of restarting or discarding partial work. Re-read the full original execution directive and complete every AC, with no false Windows/Linux qualification, no edits outside the isolated task worktree, and no commit/staging/publish.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-7fdc12, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-7fdc12)\nDEVELOPER HANDOFF 2026-07-29: Swift driver-pair contract designed and measured; ready for review. Load-bearing call: SwiftPM is rejected in its entirety, because reading what a package declares executes it (dump-package ran the manifest under both sandbox settings; the escape write landed with --disable-sandbox) and tools-version returns only the line-1 comment. The driver drives swiftc directly, enumerates Sources/**/*.swift itself, and binds only the first line of Package.swift as metadata. Closure: four executables (swiftc/swift are symlinks to one swift-frontend; clang; ld via clang -print-prog-name) all inside one fingerprinted root, plus a data-only SDK. Measured 0 PATH resolutions with a FIRING control (-use-ld=lld -> 2 hits), so the zero is earned. Second finding: external macro plugin paths derive from -sdk, so the declared Xcode SDK path puts a swift-plugin-server outside every fingerprinted root into the closure; the manager presents the SDK through a directory it owns and additionally VERIFIES every job executable and plugin path from the swiftc -### plan it is about to run. Refines TASK-260729-rhjxtx finding 6 rather than contradicting it: the frontend job spawns under a compile-only vector, not under this driver linking vector. Probe swift-boundary-fixture-v1: 20/20 cases, 32 closure checks with 0 verdicts, 6/6 controls red, 18 structural checks, green, exit 0; degraded run 20 not_run exit 0. Decision numbered 0011 because 0009 is contested (rust + hardened-profile) and 0010 is claimed by kotlin. Expected-red gates attributed: curator gofmt/make check fail only on other tasks scratch trees (0 files from this task, no tracked file modified); spec validate.py fails only its link check on 3 links inside copied docs whose targets do not exist at 57c1f56, clean baseline exits 0, scoped check over the two authored documents is 6 links / 0 broken. Nothing staged, committed, pinned or published; nothing installed on any host.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-7fdc12, pid=21861, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Swift driver-pair contract and replay the probe; do not edit producer artifacts. Challenge the central decision to reject SwiftPM and invoke swiftc directly: prove no available SwiftPM metadata query avoids executing Package.swift, and that total manager enumeration of Sources is compatible with decision 0008 rather than an unbound package-selected unit. Verify exact graph/compile argv equality, fail-closed parsing of swiftc -### output, no package code execution or mutation during planning, and complete rejection of Package.swift dependencies/plugins/macros/binary/system targets, response files, module maps, bridging headers, imports, package-selected flags/toolchains/env/network. Treat manager-owned SDK presentation and macro closure as load-bearing: test symlink/TOCTOU/path derivation, every plugin/load/server argument, external #Predicate-style macros, in-process toolchain macros, and ensure all executable/plugin bytes resolve within fingerprinted roots while SDK remains data-only. Recheck swiftc/swift-frontend/clang/ld process closure, target/runtime-library admission, canonical tools-version classifier and all cross-feed exclusions, output-path identity, local/external equivalence, cache/signing boundaries and macOS-arm64-only claim. Reproduce all six expected-red controls and gates; publish an exact ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route accordingly.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-63a4dd, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-63a4dd)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 VERDICT 2026-07-29: CHANGES REQUESTED. The central direct-swiftc architecture and SwiftPM rejection are supported: independent describe/show-dependencies/show-executables/show-traits/dump-package runs all executed Package.swift, and the probe replayed green at 20/20 cases, 32 closure checks, 6/6 expected-red controls and 18/18 structural checks. Acceptance is withheld for four implementation-readiness gaps: (1) the normative first-line-only Package.swift rule contradicts classifier scanForHeader over later lines; (2) the -### parser silently ignores malformed/non-absolute lines and missing values, uses lexical rather than resolved containment, and has no adversarial symlink/TOCTOU controls; (3) no total collision-safe Swift module-name mapping exists for protocol-valid keys with dots, hyphens, leading digits or overlength; (4) response files, scripts/unsafeFlags/configurations and the four-vs-five-member Windows closure are not explicitly closed. Full evidence and required rework: TASK-260728-1yhuqi_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. Route to analysis for decision/reference/probe revision and another reviewer cycle.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-63a4dd, pid=72180, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE 2026-07-29: Preserve the independently supported direct-swiftc architecture and SwiftPM rejection, then close exactly four acceptance gaps from TASK-260728-1yhuqi_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. Reconcile the normative first-line Package.swift rule with scanForHeader so one canonical classifier has no later-line ambiguity. Make swiftc -### parsing fail closed on every malformed/non-absolute/unknown/missing-value record; resolve and bind every executable/plugin path with adversarial symlink and TOCTOU controls before execution. Define a total deterministic collision-safe Swift module-name mapping for every protocol-valid key, including dots, hyphens, leading digits and overlength inputs, and bind it into artifact/cache/receipt identity. Explicitly close response files, scripts, unsafeFlags, configurations and the Windows four-vs-five executable closure without claiming Windows qualification. Revise decision/reference/vectors/probe, replay expected-red controls and all gates, attach cycle-1 rework evidence, and return to-review. No stage, commit, publish, pin or host install.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-63be8f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-63be8f)\nREWORK CYCLE 1 COMPLETE 2026-07-29: All four acceptance gaps from TASK-260728-1yhuqi_review-verdict-cycle-1.md closed; the independently supported direct-swiftc architecture and SwiftPM rejection are preserved unchanged. (1) Metadata rule reconciled by making the classifier read line 1 and nothing else and removing scanForHeader; a specification below line 1 is rejected-absent-header, F grows 7